# Custom Field Namespace Prefix: TI_Fnt_ (MANDATORY)

Every NEWLY GENERATED custom field API name in this project must use the form:

    TI_Fnt_<Component>__c

- Prefix: `TI_Fnt_` (exact case — not `TI_FnT_`, `TI_FNT_`, or `TI_LOGI_`).
- Suffix: `__c` (per the field-api-naming rule).
- Example: `TI_Fnt_SalesOrganization__c`, `TI_Fnt_Incoterms__c`.

## Rules

1. Apply the prefix only ONCE — never `TI_Fnt_TI_Fnt_…`. If a component already
   begins with `TI_Fnt_`, do not add it again.
2. Do NOT prefix or rename STANDARD fields (`Id`, `Name`, `OwnerId`,
   `CreatedDate`, `custom == false`, etc.) — leave them untouched.
3. Do NOT re-prefix fields that already exist in the org with a different, valid
   API name; the prefix applies to fields we are naming for the first time.
4. Length budget: the FULL name including `TI_Fnt_` (7) and `__c` (3) must be
   <= 40 chars, so the component has ~30 chars. Shorten the component sensibly
   (accepted abbreviations, drop filler) if it overflows — flag, never truncate
   mid-word.
5. Full name must match `^TI_Fnt_[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9]*__c$` and be unique within
   the object (case-insensitive).

## Note on existing conventions

Some existing objects/fields in the org use other prefixes (`TI_Logi_`,
`TI_STC_`) or none at all. This rule governs fields WE generate for this
project; if a target object's existing fields follow a different convention,
surface that to the user before applying, but default to `TI_Fnt_`.

Writing names into the Google Sheet remains gated by the sheet-write
confirmation rule.
